Subject: [PATCH 3/8] feat: a context column that disappears when it has
 nothing to say
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The rail is composed by the page, not by a parallel route slot, and the
local Next docs are why: a soft navigation keeps a slot's last active
subpage when the new route has no match, so the home's rail would follow
the reader into an empty section. The alternative -- a null page per
rail-less route -- is the guard-per-page shape this repository refuses.
WorkspaceColumns takes a ReactNode and returns its children untouched when
that node is null, so an absent rail is an absent column rather than an
empty one.

It is sticky rather than an overflow container. Next skips sticky and
fixed elements when it looks for the scroll target, so the document stays
the scroll axis and browser restoration, hash anchors and the phone's URL
bar keep working. It enters at xl, not lg: at 1024 the sidebar already
takes 17rem and a third column would leave the workspace under 500px.

"Quem está no projeto" moved out of the middle of /projeto and into the
rail. Moved, not copied. Team answers "who do I talk to", which is a
question that accompanies the whole page instead of interrupting the
journey halfway down.

Cycle and stage are deliberately not in the rail: both are already in the
main column on both pages, and the same sentence twice on one screen is
the noise phase 8 already refused. What the rail carries is what the main
column does not say -- since when the project exists, and who is on it.

